  "answer": "This has been reported before. Shortcut Guide still shows the old Windows 10 shortcut list and hasn't been updated for Windows 11, so newer shortcuts and changed ones are missing or wrong. The maintainers said it is known and tracked in the older issue #179. There is no workaround or fix in the archive for this, so follow #179 for progress. Win+, (peek at desktop) does work in Windows itself; it is only the guide's list that is out of date. Note that in a 2019 ticket (#299) the Win+, peek was described as working as intended while the Win key is held, which is a separate behavior."
